  "answer": "A balanced chemical equation provides several important pieces of information. First, it tells us about the reactants and products involved in the reaction through their chemical symbols and formulae. Second, it gives the ratio of molecules of reactants and products, which helps in understanding the stoichiometry of the reaction. Third, it provides the relative masses of the reactants and products, which is useful for calculating mass relationships. Fourth, if gases are involved, it allows us to equate their masses to their volumes and calculate the volumes of gases liberated under specific conditions of temperature and pressure. Additionally, it gives information about the number of molecules and atoms of different substances involved in the reaction, using molar mass and Avogadro’s number. Finally, it can also indicate the physical states of the substances, heat changes (exothermic or endothermic), gas evolved, or precipitate formed.",
